 helps us to be karma and so I  really think there's a place for that in  your workouts as well  so you can find a example routine and  entire workouts over at the Bonilla comm  I'll put the link to that in the  description down below but you'll notice  that that's actually already slightly  different than the push day I just did  and so of course whilst I've wanted to  share with you an example the point of  this program and of this video is that  you need to adapt it to suit your  lifestyle and also just keep changing it  keep mixing up because variety is really  what keeps the body adapting and growing  and staying challenged obviously the  martial arts training we're getting at  the end of our workouts because we're  doing them during the push day for  instance but I also would highly  recommend doing a fifth day of some kind  of martial arts class in the week if you  can and if not then you can train on  your own I recommend watching grants  video on how to do that but you will  want some tuition to give you the right  technique to start with so that you're  honing and improving the correct  technique instead of the wrong technique  of course we also need a warm up and a  cool down I recommend doing foam rolling  or self myofascial release as your  warmup maybe some dynamic stretching and  I also recommend doing a body scan  meditation which I talked a little bit  about in my fashio video I'm gonna talk  about more in the future but it'll just  help to get you calm getting the right  state of mind for the workout whilst at  the same time increasing your mind  muscle connection highly recommended and  then at the end you can just do some  stretching because flexibility is also  important but we're also going to do  that on our D load week and one more  thing I also recommend that on your  fourth week you take a week off you take  a deal ode week and during this time I'm  not just gonna be sitting around you're  gonna do all that other Batman stuff  you're gonna 