g routine  and that's going to involve meditation  image streaming writing with your left  hand in a journal and dual n-back  training but again I'll go into all this  in more detail in a future if that  sounds like something you'd like to hear  about  so if you only take one thing from this  I want it to be those dynamic drop sets  so just to properly explain once again  what that is basically a drop set is  where you keep going by lowering the  weight a mechanical drop set might mean  that you're changing exercise safe and  bench press to press ups the dynamic  drop set means that you're combining  both those things but you might also be  changing up the cadence for instance by  going from a overcoming isometric or  very slow five to five rhythm to a  faster more explosive rhythm within the  same set and then to extend that I want  you to think about your entire workout  as some kind of giant drop set so that  you're moving from more complex moves to  more isolated moves to the or mixing up  your rest time so that you're throwing  the hold three times ten out of the  window and one more way to explain this  is as a way to combine the three  triggers of games the muscle damage the  mechanical tension and the metabolic  stress so doing something like planche  is fantastic for mechanical tension but  you can't do it enough to cause the kind  of hypertrophy that you get from  metabolic stress so by combining two  different types of exercise by dropping  from something more complex and then  isolating a specific muscle when it's  already fatigued you're able to do both  of those things and over on the website  you'll find complete programs that you  can start using but the whole point of  this isn't that you follow those  training programs to a tee although you  can do that and I'd love to know your  progress if you do please share but that  you adapt these routines and you keep  changing them to fit your lifestyle and  also your circumstances there are ways  that you 